\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Speed Thy servants, Saviour, speed them;
\par Thou art Lord of winds and waves:
\par They were bound, but Thou hast freed them;
\par Now they go to free the slaves.
\par Be Thou with them:
\par 'Tis Thine arm alone that saves.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Friends, and home, and all forsaking,
\par Lord, they go at Thy command;
\par As their stay Thy promise taking,
\par While they traverse sea and land:
\par O be with them!
\par Lead them safely by the hand.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. When they reach the land of strangers,
\par And the prospect dark appears,
\par Nothing seen but toils and dangers,
\par Nothing felt but doubts and fears,
\par Be Thou with them,
\par Hear their sighs and count their tears.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Where no fruit appears to cheer them,
\par And they seem to toil in vain,
\par Then in mercy, Lord, draw near them,
\par Then their sinking hopes sustain;
\par Thus supported,
\par Let their zeal revive again.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. In the midst of opposition,
\par Let them trust, O Lord, in Thee;
\par When success attend their mission,
\par Let Thy servant humbler be;
\par Never leave them,
\par Till Thy face in heaven they see:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. There to reap in joy for ever
\par Fruit that grows from seed here sown,
\par There to be with Him who never
\par Ceases to preserve His own,
\par And with gladness
\par Give the praise to Him alone.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

